{"version": 1, "sourceSha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "documents": [{"id": "offline-ee76992c5948cf05479d", "filename": "READING 19.pdf", "sha256": "ee76992c5948cf05479db8d2457b7f9f0219ecb466be531233f561030c5cff8f", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/ee76992c5948cf05479db8d2457b7f9f0219ecb466be531233f561030c5cff8f.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/ee76992c5948cf05479db8d2457b7f9f0219ecb466be531233f561030c5cff8f.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "units": [{"id": "ee76992c5948cf05-p1", "label": "Part A · READING 19.pdf", "part": "A", "sourceSha256": "ee76992c5948cf05479db8d2457b7f9f0219ecb466be531233f561030c5cff8f", "pages": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], "questions": [{"number": 1, "prompt": "A rare disease condition, peculiarly begins at very early age.\nAnswer_____________.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 395, "answer": {"text": "C", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 2, "prompt": ".Diagnosis is based on the presence of primary lymphoedema and distichiasis.\nAnswer_____________.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 484, "answer": {"text": "D", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 3, "prompt": "Disorder is passed down (inherited) through families.\nAnswer____________.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 587, "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 4, "prompt": ".A condition characterized by an excess of watery fluid collecting in the cavities\nor tissues of the body.\nAnswer____________.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 667, "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 5, "prompt": "It can be said that approximately 75% of affected individuals have an affected\nparent.\nAnswer_____________.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 799, "answer": {"text": "D", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 6, "prompt": "No proper statistics are available.\nAnswer____________.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 913, "answer": {"text": "A", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 7, "prompt": "Classically affects lower half of the legs only.\nAnswer____________.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 974, "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 8, "prompt": "What can occur as a part of more complex syndromic disorder?\nAnswer____________.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 152, "answer": {"text": "Primary impairment of the lymphatic drainage system", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 9, "prompt": "What is suggestive of a diagnosis of lymphoedema distichiasis?\nAnswer___________.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 240, "answer": {"text": "A lymphoscintigram showing lymph reflux", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 10, "prompt": "Which syndrome is inherited in an autosomal dominant manner?\nAnswer__________.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 329, "answer": {"text": "Lymphoedema-distichiasis syndrome", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 11, "prompt": ".What is that Greek Word which may mean “Two Rows?”\nAnswer__________.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 416, "answer": {"text": "Distichiasis", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 12, "prompt": "What is the percentage of recurrence risk for family members if one of the\nparents carries the gene?\nAnswer____________.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 493, "answer": {"text": "50%", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 13, "prompt": "Which Greek or Latin Word may mean “From The Beginning?\nAnswer__________.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 622, "answer": {"text": "De novo", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 14, "prompt": "Which syndrome can also present with cardiac abnormalities?\nAnswer___________.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 704, "answer": {"text": "Lymphoedema-distichiasis syndrome", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 17, "prompt": "In absence of distichiasis, it could be difficult to find_____________ in the\ncausative gene.", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 297, "answer": {"text": "mutation", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "Conservative management of _____________ is with lubrication or epilation.", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 396, "answer": {"text": "Conservative management of symptomatic distichiasis", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 19, "prompt": ".__________ may not surface itself in an apparent way.", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 476, "answer": {"text": "symptomatic distichiasis", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "It is advisable that ___________ shall undergo testing as this can minimize risk\nof transfer of genes", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 535, "answer": {"text": "parents", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "ee76992c5948cf05-p7", "label": "Part B · PART B", "part": "B", "sourceSha256": "ee76992c5948cf05479db8d2457b7f9f0219ecb466be531233f561030c5cff8f", "pages": [7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12], "questions": [{"number": 1, "prompt": "As per information given in the table, to define NAFLD;\nA Evidence of hepatic steatosis both by histology and imaging is required.\nB Secondary causes of hepatic fat accumulation needed to be taken into\nconsideration.\nC Monogenic hereditary disorder gets revealed.\nNAFLD\nIn the majority of patients, NAFLD is commonly associated with metabolic\ncomorbidities such as obesity, diabetes mellitus, and dyslipidemia. NAFLD can be\ncategorized histologically into nonalcoholic fatty liver (NAFL) or nonalcoholic\nsteatohepatitis. NAFL is defined as the presence of 5% HS without evidence of\nhepatocellular injury in the form of hepatocyte ballooning (e.g., ballooning), with\nor without any fibrosis. A not-so common form of\nmonogenic disorder but the underlying genetic defect is expressed .", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 224, "answer": {"text": "C Monogenic hereditary disorder gets revealed.", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 3, "prompt": "What is right about risks, specific to Laparoscopic Splenectomy?\nA Swelling on the stomach.\nB May damage lungs completely.\nC Blood vessels may rupture.\nRisks Involved\nInjury to the tail of the pancreas, resulting in a collection of fluid in the abdomen\nthat may require a further operation or drainage procedures.\nBleeding from the blood vessels that flow to the spleen requiring a return to the\noperating theatre.\nSignificant distention of the stomach that may lead to a large vomit. Occasionally\nsome of this vomit may be inhaled into the lungs and cause life threatening\npneumonia. This is why a tube will be placed via your nose into the stomach for\nthe first day after the operation.\nSplenunculi. Many people have tiny `extra` spleens. After the spleen is removed\nthey may grow and patients with blood diseases may have a recurrence of their\ndisease. This may require further surgery.\nBecause the spleen is very close to the lung, collapse of the left lung, to some\nmeasure, is quite common after splenectomy. A physiotherapist will work with you\nto prevent this. It is very common to have a slight fever on the first 1 – 2 days after\nthe operation because of this lung collapse.", "sourcePage": 9, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "A Swelling on the stomach.", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 6, "prompt": "What does the word sepsis mean?\nA Life-threatening complication arising due to infection.\nB Indicates release of chemicals into the bloodstream to fight the infection.\nC Higher death risk arising due to infection\nPediatric Trauma\nThe field has made major advances in the areas of sepsis, lung injury, traumatic\nbrain injury and postoperative care. The pediatric intensives role in the Trauma\nEvents is to give steady care during cardiorespiratory or multi-organ failure or\nrecuperation from surgical medications or a traumatic injury that happens to an\ninfant, child or adolescent. It manages the medicinal consideration of infants,\nchildren, and teenagers, and as far as possible as a rule ranges from birth up to 18\nyears old. It is a zone inside a healing center, spends significant time in the\nconsideration of critically ill infants and children. The risk of death for injured\nchildren is significantly lower when care is provided in pediatric trauma, which\nfocuses as opposed than non-pediatric trauma which is incorporated into the\nCritical Care Meetings.", "sourcePage": 12, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "A Life-threatening complication arising due to infection.", "source": {"id": "offline-f23101fffc0e717a4fa3", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 19.pdf", "sha256": "f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f23101fffc0e717a4fa3240d65b710f1dbeb8c6c473442e8837daa40c0f5e3ba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills"